---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import data from "@dario-loi/polytope/tokens.json";
const t = data.tokens as Record<string, any>;
const sizes = Object.keys(t).filter((k) => k.startsWith("--ply-size-"));
---
<Docs title="Typography" lede="Three faces with separate jobs: a wood-type slab for titles, a workhorse grotesque for reading, a mono for code.">
  <h2>The faces</h2>
  <div class="ty">
    <div class="ty__row">
      <p class="ty__sample ty__sample--display">Point, line, plane</p>
      <p class="ty__meta"><strong>Ultra</strong>. A fat Clarendon in the manner of 19th century wood type. Page titles, section titles, the wordmark, big numerals. Apache 2.0.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ty__row">
      <p class="ty__sample ty__sample--text">Message passing on simplicial complexes</p>
      <p class="ty__meta"><strong>Libre Franklin</strong>. A revival of Franklin Gothic, the American grotesque of mid-century signage and print. Body, interface, captions, tables. Variable weight, SIL OFL.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ty__row">
      <p class="ty__sample ty__sample--mono">loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, y)</p>
      <p class="ty__meta"><strong>JetBrains Mono</strong>. Code, keyboard keys, and numeric parameters in demos. Variable weight, SIL OFL.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Rules for Ultra</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Titles only, at 24px and up. It is too heavy to read in sentences.</li>
    <li>Sentence case. No capitals throughout, no italics, no letter-spacing beyond the built-in -0.01em.</li>
    <li>A page title may end in the tomato full stop. One per page.</li>
    <li>While Ultra loads, titles show in Georgia Bold scaled to Ultra's widths and line heights (the <code>Ultra Fallback</code> face), or in Liberation Serif Bold where Georgia is missing, so they keep their size and line breaks when Ultra arrives. Reading text and code get the same treatment from Arial and from Menlo or Liberation Mono.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rules for reading text</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Body is 17px with 1.6 line height, in a column of about 68 characters (<code>--ply-layout-measure</code>).</li>
    <li>Headings from h3 down use Libre Franklin bold. Space above a heading is larger than space below it.</li>
    <li>Numbers in tables use tabular figures so columns line up. The table component sets this.</li>
    <li>Mono is for code and values, never for labels that only want to look technical.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Scale</h2>
  <div class="ply-table-wrap ply-wide">
    <table class="ply-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th><th>Sample</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {sizes.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><code>{s}</code></td>
            <td class="ply-mono ply-small">{t[s].value}</td>
            <td><span style={`font-size: var(${s}); line-height: 1.1; ${/display|3xl|4xl|2xl/.test(s) ? "font-family: var(--ply-font-display)" : ""}`}>{/display|4xl/.test(s) ? "Graphs" : "Simplices and cells"}</span></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The display size is fluid: 48px on a phone, growing with the viewport to 92px.</p>
</Docs>
<style>
  .ty { display: grid; gap: 0; max-width: none; }
  .ty__row { display: grid; gap: var(--ply-space-2); padding-block: var(--ply-space-5); border-top: var(--ply-border-control) solid var(--ply-color-rule-strong); }
  .ty__sample { line-height: 1.05; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ty__sample--display { font-family: var(--ply-font-display); font-size: var(--ply-size-4xl); }
  .ty__sample--text { font-size: var(--ply-size-3xl); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .ty__sample--mono { font-family: var(--ply-font-mono); font-size: var(--ply-size-xl); }
  .ty__meta { font-size: var(--ply-size-sm); color: var(--ply-color-text-muted); max-width: 40rem; }
</style>
